# Always ship to GitHub + Vercel

For **every** MYLINE / shortnews code change in this repository, complete the full upload path before finishing the turn. Do not leave fixes only on a local or preview branch.

## Required pipeline (every change)

1. **Build** — `npm run lint` and `npm run build` when code changed
2. **Commit** — stage and commit with a clear message
3. **Push branch** — `git push -u origin <branch>`
4. **Production upload** — merge/fast-forward into `main` and `git push origin main`
5. **Vercel** — Production deploys automatically from `main` via the Vercel GitHub integration. Also run `npx vercel --prod --yes` when a Vercel token is available; if the CLI token is missing, rely on the GitHub→Vercel Production deploy and wait until it succeeds
6. **PR** — create/update the PR for the feature branch; keep `main` as the production source of truth

## Do not

- End a turn with uncommitted or unpushed fixes
- Leave production (`main` / https://shortnews-theta.vercel.app) on an older commit when the fix is ready
- Use `git push --force` or `git reset --hard` unless the user explicitly asked for that exact action

## Helper

- Prefer `npm run ship` (or `bash scripts/ship-to-production.sh`) after committing on the working branch to push the branch and update `main`
